From 4f507b1804f1660468a34df67fd5475f1be1ff63 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Alvaro Figueroa <alvarof@microsoft.com>
Date: Fri, 25 Sep 2026 18:38:31 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] espressif: add Meshnology W12

ESP32-S3R8 (8 MB octal PSRAM) with 16 MB flash, a Semtech LR2021
dual-band LoRa radio, an SSD1315 OLED behind VEXT_ENABLE and an L76K
GNSS. Heltec V3-style pinout, taken from meshtastic/firmware
variants/esp32s3/meshnology-w12.

Enables CIRCUITPY_ENABLE_MPY_NATIVE: the LR2021 driver and the
meshtastic codec ship as native .mpy files and the loader rejects them
without it.

USB PID 0xFED2 under Espressif's VID. The board ships without a UF2
bootloader; cpy-meshtastic builds TinyUF2 for it, which enumerates with
the same VID/PID and uses the same 16 MB partition layout as this
port's partitions-16MB.csv.

Carried by cpy-meshtastic in temp-board-patches/ until the board is in
the tree it builds against.
